WHAT IS AND IS NOT CLAIMED

The copyright claimed here covers this particular implementation — the source
code, its structure, and its documentation.

It does NOT claim ownership of the scientific models the Software implements.
Those are published, publicly available science, and anyone is free to
implement them independently. They include, among others: the PVWatts v5 DC
model, the Sandia module temperature model, the PSA solar position algorithm
(Blanco-Muriel et al. 2001), Liu & Jordan isotropic transposition (1963), the
Haurwitz clear-sky model (1945), Passias & Kallback row shading (1984), the
ASHRAE incidence angle modifier, the Kimber soiling model (2014), Kasten &
Young air mass (1989), IEC 61724-1 performance ratio, the Henyey-Greenstein
phase function (1941), and the real-time volumetric rendering techniques
described by Schneider & Vos (SIGGRAPH 2015), Jimenez (2014) and Mitchell
(GPU Gems 3).

